  "id": "cremmer_scherk",
  "name": "Cremmer-Scherk Spontaneous Compactification",
  "short_name": "Cremmer-Scherk",
  "description": "Minkowski space times a sphere, in six dimensions: the solution of gravity coupled to gauge fields with which Eugene Cremmer and Joël Scherk showed in 1976 that extra dimensions can curl up by the field equations. A magnetic monopole field through the sphere holds it open at one radius, and a cosmological constant of six dimensions keeps the other four dimensions flat.",
